        <p>No cap: every generation thinks the next generation is ruining the language. The Baby Boomers hated "groovy." Generation X was told that saying "radical" was destroying the English language. Millennials received serious criticism for using "literally" as an intensifier and "adulting" as a verb. And now Gen Z slang - rizz, slay, ate, bussin, it's giving, understood the assignment, no cap, rent free, main character - is being written about in worried opinion pieces as evidence of linguistic decline, intellectual laziness, or the general deterioration of culture.</p>
